---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Corrections" description="How to request a correction from Oropis.">
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Accountability</p>
    <h1>Corrections</h1>
    <p>We would rather fix a story than defend a mistake.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap narrow prose">
    <h2>How to flag an error</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:abhishek.shinde@oropis.com">abhishek.shinde@oropis.com</a> with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The article URL.</li>
      <li>The exact sentence or claim that is wrong.</li>
      <li>What the correct information is, with a primary source if possible.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What happens next</h2>
    <p>We review the source and the published copy. Confirmed factual errors are corrected promptly. When the change is substantive, the article carries a correction note with the date. Typos and formatting fixes are made without a note.</p>

    <h2>Clarifications</h2>
    <p>If a sentence is technically accurate but misleading, we may add a clarification rather than rewrite the record. The goal is to make the story right, not to erase the fact that it changed.</p>

    <h2>Disagreements</h2>
    <p>We do not remove accurate reporting because a subject dislikes it. We do correct facts, add context, and publish a response when a subject provides one on the record.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
